# 15. The actual build prompt

You can give this to an AI coding agent:

Build an MVP SaaS product called **FlowForge DocumentFlow**.

## Product

FlowForge DocumentFlow is an AI-powered document processing and workflow automation platform for businesses.

The initial use case is invoice processing.

The system should allow a business to upload or submit invoices, extract structured information using AI, validate the information, apply configurable business rules, send uncertain/high-value invoices for human approval, and export approved data to an external system.

The product must emphasize reliability, auditability, human oversight, and measurable ROI.

## Target user

Small and medium-sized businesses with repetitive document-processing workflows and limited internal automation resources.

Primary user roles:

* Organization owner
* Administrator
* Operations user
* Approver

## MVP features

### 1. Authentication

Implement:

* Sign up
* Login
* Logout
* Password reset
* Organization creation
* Basic role-based permissions

### 2. Dashboard

Display:

* Total documents processed
* Documents automatically completed
* Documents requiring review
* Exceptions
* Automation percentage
* Estimated hours saved
* Estimated cost savings
* Recent workflow activity

### 3. Document Inbox

Users must be able to:

* Upload PDF invoices
* Upload image invoices
* View document status
* Search documents
* Filter by status
* Open individual documents

Statuses:

* Uploaded
* Processing
* Review required
* Approved
* Rejected
* Completed
* Failed

### 4. AI extraction

For each invoice, extract:

* Vendor name
* Invoice number
* Invoice date
* Due date
* Currency
* Subtotal
* Tax
* Total
* Purchase order number
* Line items

Every extracted field must have:

* Value
* Confidence score

The system must never silently invent missing information.

If information cannot be confidently extracted, flag it for review.

### 5. Invoice review

Create a split-screen review interface.

Left side:

* Invoice/document preview

Right side:

* Extracted fields
* Confidence scores
* Validation warnings

Allow users to:

* Edit fields
* Approve
* Reject
* Submit for further review

Record every change in an audit log.

### 6. Workflow engine

Implement a simple workflow engine.

Example workflow:

WHEN an invoice is received:

1. Extract information.
2. Validate required fields.
3. Check invoice amount.
4. If amount is below configured threshold, continue automatically.
5. If amount exceeds threshold, require human approval.
6. After approval, export the invoice data.
7. Mark the workflow as completed.

Make thresholds configurable by organization administrators.

### 7. Approval Center

Create a page showing all items requiring human attention.

Each item must display:

* Document
* Amount
* Vendor
* Reason for review
* AI confidence
* Date received

Actions:

* Approve
* Reject
* Edit

### 8. Integrations

For the MVP implement:

* CSV export
* Google Sheets integration
* Generic webhook

Design the architecture so additional integrations can be added later.

### 9. ROI dashboard

Track:

* Number of documents processed
* Estimated manual processing time
* Actual automated processing time
* Hours saved
* Estimated labor savings
* Automation percentage

Allow administrators to configure an estimated manual processing cost/hour.

Clearly label ROI values as estimates.

### 10. Audit log

Record:

* User actions
* AI extraction events
* Workflow events
* Approvals
* Rejections
* Data edits
* Integration events
* Errors

Include timestamps and user IDs where applicable.

## UI/UX

Create a professional B2B SaaS interface.

Design principles:

* Clean
* Minimal
* Professional
* Fast
* Easy to understand
* Responsive
* Desktop-first but mobile-friendly

Main navigation:

Dashboard
Documents
Approvals
Workflows
Integrations
Analytics
Settings

## Security

Implement:

* Organization-level data isolation
* Role-based access
* Secure authentication
* Secure document storage
* Server-side authorization
* Audit logging
* Input validation
* File type validation
* File size limits

Never expose API keys or secrets to the client.

## Architecture

Use:

Frontend:
Next.js + React + Tailwind CSS

Backend:
Use Next.js server/API routes or a clean backend architecture.

Database:
PostgreSQL

Storage:
S3-compatible object storage.

AI:
Use an LLM/API capable of structured JSON extraction.

Design all external AI and integration calls behind service abstractions so providers can be replaced later.

## Database

Create tables/models for:

users
organizations
organization_members
documents
document_extractions
workflows
workflow_steps
workflow_runs
approvals
integrations
audit_logs
roi_metrics

Include appropriate indexes, foreign keys, timestamps, and organization-level access controls.

## Important AI behavior

The AI must return structured data.

Never allow the model to directly execute arbitrary business actions.

The workflow engine must determine what actions are allowed.

AI should provide:

* extracted information
* classification
* confidence
* suggested decisions

Deterministic business rules should control execution.

Human approval must be available for uncertain or high-risk cases.

## Demo mode

Create seeded demo data so a new user can immediately see:

* Example invoices
* Completed workflows
* Pending approvals
* Dashboard metrics
* ROI calculations

Include a demo invoice containing:

Vendor: ABC Supplies Ltd
Invoice Number: INV-2048
Total: ₦1,450,000
Currency: NGN

Also include at least one invoice that exceeds an approval threshold and therefore requires human review.

## Product goal

The MVP should communicate one simple value proposition:

"FlowForge takes repetitive document workflows off your team's hands and turns them into measurable, AI-powered automation."

Do not build unnecessary features.

Prioritize a reliable end-to-end invoice workflow over breadth.

The final application should be runnable locally, have clear environment-variable documentation, database migration/seed scripts, and basic automated tests for authentication, document processing, workflow rules, approval flow, and organization-level data isolation.

### The strategic move

**Don't build the entire FlowForge vision first.**

Build **DocumentFlow → get 3–5 businesses using it → measure the ROI → charge them → identify the next workflow they want automated.**

Then DocumentFlow becomes the first module of the larger **FlowForge Automation Platform**, rather than a standalone dead-end product.
